      "hints": [
        "Find $x^2$ coefficient: $a = \\binom{6}{2}(3^4)(-2)^2 = 4860$.",
        "Find $x^3$ coefficient: $b = \\binom{6}{3}(3^3)(-2)^3 = -4320$.",
        "Calculate $\\frac{a}{b} = \\frac{4860}{-4320} = -\\frac{9}{8}$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Extract the coefficient $a$ of $x^2$ from the binomial expansion of $(3 - 2x)^6$:\n$$a = \\binom{6}{2}(3^4)(-2)^2 = 15 \\times 81 \\times 4 = 4860$$",
        "Extract the coefficient $b$ of $x^3$ from the binomial expansion:\n$$b = \\binom{6}{3}(3^3)(-2)^3 = 20 \\times 27 \\times (-8) = -4320$$",
        "Compute the ratio $\\frac{a}{b}$ in simplest fractional form:\n$$\\frac{a}{b} = \\frac{4860}{-4320} = -\\frac{486}{432} = -\\frac{9}{8} \\quad (=-1.125)$$"
      ],
